-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Fourth Term Split Close Once Commuted
-- statement:
--   **The fourth term is within the commutation square root of its once-commuted split form.**
--
--   Let `psi_bi` be normalized and assume the left and right switcheroo point-product families satisfy an `SDDOpRel` bound with error `chi`. If $T_4$ is the named fourth aggregate term and $S_{\mathrm{once}}$ is the average of the split product with complete-part total, `M` outcome, and family outcome factors, then
--
--   $$
--   \left|T_4-S_{\mathrm{once}}\right|\le\sqrt{\chi}.
--   $$
--
--   The proof uses the split-by-`g` identity and the projective sandwich contraction. This is the first square-root `chi` step in the fourth-term switcheroo chain.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateFourthTerm_split_close_once_commuted`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
